course: dictionary
lesson: 5071
title: Instinct: born, not taught
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An instinct is something you are born with. You do not need to learn it. «Birds build nests by instinct.» Nobody teaches a bird how to build a nest, so the words «by instinct» tell you it knows how naturally.
explain: «Cats are hunters by instinct» means hunting comes from inside the cat, from its wild ancestors, even when it is well fed. The clue is «even when well fed»: the cat hunts because it is born with the urge, not because it is hungry.
explain: Instinct can also mean a strong feeling about what is right or wrong. In safety lessons, «trust your instinct» means that if something feels wrong, you should listen to that uneasy feeling, get away and tell a trusted adult.
fact: Instinct means a natural way of behaving that an animal or person is born with.
fact: Learned behaviour is the opposite of instinct: it has to be taught.
fact: «Babies grasp fingers» without being taught, because it is instinct.
fact: «Hunting animals have a strong instinct to chase things that run away.»
fact: Useful phrases: by instinct, gut instinct, survival instinct, instinctive.
exercise: «Birds build nests by instinct.» What does this tell you about nest building? | *It is something birds are born knowing how to do | It is only done in summer | It is a kind of song | It is learned from parents
exercise: In a safety lesson, what does «trust your instinct» mean? | Wait an hour before you think about it | *Listen to a strong feeling that something is wrong, then get away and tell a trusted adult | Do what your friends do | Ignore any uneasy feeling
exercise: Which one is learned, not instinct? | *Reading a book with a teacher | Baby turtles heading to the sea | Spiders spinning webs | Babies grasping fingers
test: What is the difference between instinct and learned behaviour? | *Instinct is born in you; learned behaviour is taught | Learned behaviour is born in you | They mean exactly the same | Instinct is always taught at school
test: What does «by instinct» mean in «Birds build nests by instinct»? | Sadly | Quickly, in a rush | *Naturally, without being taught | Carefully, after a lesson
exam: Which sentence uses instinct to mean a natural talent? | Lunch is an instinct. | The cat ate its instinct for dinner. | We instinct the bus home. | *She has an instinct for music.
